From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:38:12 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 194/207] dsv41 runner: answer-commit beside the compute lane's
 built-in tool

A request that offers only the lane's built-in python tool (code_interpreter)
may now commit: the commit fires inside the think block, so no call is in
progress, and the lane's hold at the commit's EOS finds no call in the
answer and ends the reply there. Any tool the client runs still turns
commit off (its call may be the answer). The compute-lane hold no longer
turns it off by itself.
